      "title": "CGM options: fill the glucose simulator's Reset to Defaults with system blue",
      "body": "Follow-up to #1685. The glucose simulator's Reset to Defaults button is filled with `Color.accentColor`, which in the CGM sheet picks up the tab bar's lavender tint. It now uses `Color(.systemBlue)`, like Trio's other filled buttons such as Enact Bolus and the therapy editors' Save.\n\n| iPhone 17 Pro, iOS 27.2, before | iPhone 17 Pro, iOS 27.2, after |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75734d92-2b43-44b4-b2c7-3591e55c24a4\" width=\"300\" alt=\"iPhone 17 Pro on iOS 27.2, before: lavender Reset to Defaults\"> | <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edadedfd-72a3-451e-a3da-e1a2f667f9fb\" width=\"300\" alt=\"iPhone 17 Pro on iOS 27.2, after: system blue Reset to Defaults\"> |\n\n| iPhone SE, iOS 18.0, before | iPhone SE, iOS 18.0, after |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a367a6b3-b74d-49d2-885a-fa2a445af091\" width=\"300\" alt=\"iPhone SE on iOS 18.0, before: lavender Reset to Defaults\"> | <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1db972a-359a-42cd-94b8-9f37e9c6ae3e\" width=\"300\" alt=\"iPhone SE on iOS 18.0, after: system blue Reset to Defaults\"> |\n",
